  "verbalization": "Tocainide is implicated in the regulation of voltage-gated sodium channel activity through its interaction with Scn7a and Scn8a, which are both involved in the same biological process. The evidence suggests that Tocainide binds to these channels, leading to their participation in sodium channel activity, which in turn is associated with Scn3a. This chain of interactions implies that Tocainide may influence Scn3a through a shared pathway involving sodium channel activity. The consistent binding of Tocainide to Scn7a and Scn8a, both of which are linked to Scn3a, supports a mechanism where Tocainide modulates the activity of sodium channels, potentially affecting Scn3a. The overlapping roles of these channels in sodium channel activity suggest that Tocainide may exert its effects on Scn3a through a common intermediary, reinforcing the notion of a direct or indirect relationship between the two entities.",
